Note on P6: duplicate keys — I need a strict YAML loader. `yaml.compose` with a custom constructor won't raise; better to use `yaml.safe_load` with a loader subclass that overrides `construct_mapping` to detect duplicate keys. Standard recipe:

```python
class StrictLoader(yaml.SafeLoader): pass
def _no_dup(loader, node, deep=False):
    keys=[]
    for k,v in node.value:
        kk=loader.construct_object(k, deep=deep)
        if kk in keys: raise yaml.constructor.ConstructorError(...)
        keys.append(kk)
    return yaml.SafeLoader.construct_mapping(loader,node,deep)
StrictLoader.add_constructor(yaml.resolver.BaseResolver.DEFAULT_MAPPING_TAG, _no_dup)
```
